  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I'm the creator of the WorldObject prefab - https://github.com/seanedwards/vrc-worldobject - and I've noticed that when attaching physbones and contact components to objects that are underneath a WorldObject, they tend to have a lag effect when the player turns their head. \nI have a video of the effect here: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Uq_8HpZx27w\nBased on tests interacting with the object, I believe it's the bone itself that's offset from the model, not just the debug overlay.\nIt feels almost like the WorldObject (really just a parent constraint) and the physbones are being updated in the wrong order. I think it's possible that this could be a general problem with physbones applied to objects that are moved by constraints, but I have not tested this specifically.\n\nThis appears to be reproducible in editor too: https://i.gyazo.com/cda84e786bd03929fd5acc967c1c0a6b.mp4",
